#Omega-free variant of ProteinAtomRigidGroups.rbody. Use this one WITH
#--dihedral, and the standard file without it.
#
#Why it exists. A _PHI group spans the peptide bond -C-N and a _PSI group
#spans C-+N, so each puts springs between substituents on either side of an
#omega axis -- which locks it. Audited on ubiquitin, the standard file leaves
#325 of 400 rotatable bonds free and the 75 it locks are every one of the
#peptide bonds. That is the right answer when nothing else models omega: the
#peptide bond is planar and the mesh is what keeps it so.
#
#It stops being the right answer once --dihedral supplies a real omega
#torsion. The term is then applied to an axis that cannot turn: measured, it
#contributes 10.89 kJ/mol of 3009.46 on ubiquitin, and only because the
#structure already starts trans where the mesh and the torsion happen to
#agree. A structure arriving with a distorted omega could not be corrected,
#and cis/trans isomerism -- proline's in particular -- cannot be modelled at
#all.
#
#What changes. Each _PHI and _PSI group is split in two at its axis, so that
#both halves keep the two axis atoms but no half holds substituents from
#both sides. Springs from an axis atom to a substituent are 1-3 distances,
#invariant under the rotation, so they still hold their valence angle
#without constraining the torsion. Audited: 384 of 400 bonds free, no omega
#among the 16 remaining, and every valence angle still covered.
#
#Generated from ProteinAtomRigidGroups.rbody -- regenerate rather than
#hand-edit, so the two stay in step.
#

A_CA ALA N CA C CB HA
A_NTER ALA N CA H1 H H2 H3
A_CTER ALA CA C O OXT
A_PHIC  ALA -CA -C -O N
A_PHIN  ALA -C N H CA
A_PSIC  ALA CA C O +N
A_PSIN  ALA C +N +H +CA
A_CB ALA CA CB HB1 HB2 HB3

R_CA ARG N CA C CB HA
R_NTER ARG N CA H1 H H2 H3
R_CTER ARG CA C O OXT
R_PHIC  ARG -CA -C -O N
R_PHIN  ARG -C N H CA
R_PSIC  ARG CA C O +N
R_PSIN  ARG C +N +H +CA
R_CB ARG CA CB CG HB2 HB3
R_CG ARG CB CG CD HG2 HG3
R_CD ARG CG CD NE HD2 HD3
R_NE ARG CD NE CZ HE
R_CZ ARG NE CZ NH1 NH2
R_NH1 ARG CZ NH1 HH11 HH12
R_NH2 ARG CZ NH2 HH21 HH22

